<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central American Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1826–1829</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central American Civil War was fought from 1826 to 1829 within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-republic-of-central-america">Federal Republic of Central America</a> between conservatives, led by President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-jose-arce">Manuel José Arce</a>, and liberals. The liberal forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-morazan">Francisco Morazán</a> won, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala-city">Guatemala City</a> in 1829, and Morazán became federal president in 1830, though the federation broke apart within a decade.</p></div>
